<%# One post of the thread: the words, the count, an optional link, and the card that each network
    will render for that link.

    ⚠️ Both fields must render for every block, in the same order. The names are `posts[][text]`
    and `posts[][link]`, and Rails starts a new hash when a key repeats. There is no index in the
    name, on purpose: an index needs renumbering in the browser at each add and each remove. The
    tiles of the photos come AFTER those two fields, and `text` must stay the first field.
%>
<%# ⚠️ The Bluesky map is a plain data attribute and NOT a Stimulus value. Refer to
    `blueskyMentions` in social_post_controller.js. %>
<div class="social-post" data-social-target="post" data-controller="social-post"
     data-admin-i18n="<%= admin_i18n_data("admin.js.social_post", shared: "admin.js.shared") %>"
     data-social-post-bluesky-mentions="<%= mentions_json %>"
     data-social-post-preview-url-value="<%= social_preview_path %>"
     data-social-post-upload-url-value="<%= social_photos_path %>"
     data-social-post-limit-value="<%= limit %>"
     data-social-post-warn-at-value="<%= warn_at %>"
     data-social-post-max-photos-value="<%= max_photos %>"
     data-social-post-alt-limit-value="<%= alt_limit %>">

  <%# A line between two posts. It is on each block and the first one hides it, thus a block that
      the browser clones needs no extra markup. %>
  <wa-divider class="social-post__divider"></wa-divider>

  <%# ⚠️ Everything but the divider is in this wrapper, and the wrapper owns the gap between the
      fields. Without it that gap would also apply below the divider, and the space above the line
      could never match the space below it. Refer to _social.scss. %>
  <div class="social-post__body">
    <%# ⚠️ The HANDLE carries `draggable`, and never the block. A draggable block takes the pointer
        away from the fields inside it, thus a person could not select the words of their own post.
        ⚠️ It is a real button, thus the arrow keys move the post with no pointer. It is hidden
        while there is one post. %>
    <wa-button class="social-post__handle" appearance="plain" size="small" draggable="true"
               data-social-target="handle"
               data-action="dragstart->social#dragStart dragend->social#dragEnd
                            keydown->social#movePostByKey">
      <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "grip-dots-vertical") %>
      <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".reorder") %></span>
    </wa-button>

    <%# ⚠️ The icon is in the DEFAULT slot and not in `start`. With `start` and no label, the button
        keeps the width of a label that is not there.
        ⚠️ `<wa-button>` makes a square icon button only for a `<wa-icon>` child, which this app
        never uses. Thus _social.scss gives the square. It is hidden while there is one post. %>
    <wa-button class="social-post__remove" appearance="plain" size="small"
               data-social-target="remove" data-action="click->social#removePost">
      <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "circle-xmark") %>
      <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".remove") %></span>
    </wa-button>

    <%# ⚠️ No `maxlength` and no `with-count`. Both measure UTF-16 code units, and Bluesky counts
        graphemes: one emoji is 1 there and 2 or more here. The count line below is ours, and it
        warns and never stops a keystroke. %>
    <wa-textarea name="posts[][text]" label="<%= t(".body") %>" rows="5" resize="auto" required
                 value="<%= post.text %>"
                 placeholder="<%= t(".body_placeholder") %>"
                 data-social-post-target="body"
                 data-action="input->social-post#count">
    </wa-textarea>

    <%# The toolbar and the count, on one line below the words.
        ⚠️ It is a ROW of controls and not one button: a control for a photo, and each other kind of
        attachment, goes beside the link button. Thus the button is not in the count line itself. %>
    <div class="social-post__toolbar">
      <%# ⚠️ The icon is in the DEFAULT slot and _social.scss gives the square, as for the remove
          control above.
          ⚠️ It is DISABLED while the post has a link or a photo, and it is never hidden. Refer to
          `renderAttachmentState` in social_post_controller.js. %>
      <wa-button class="social-post__tool" appearance="plain" size="small"
                 data-social-post-target="linkButton"
                 data-action="click->social-post#showLink"
                 <%= "disabled" if post.link.present? || post.photos.any? %>>
        <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "link") %>
        <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".add_link") %></span>
      </wa-button>

      <%# The photo button, which opens the picker below the toolbar. ⚠️ A post takes photos OR a
          link, and not both: Bluesky renders one embed. The server renders both states. %>
      <wa-button class="social-post__tool" appearance="plain" size="small"
                 data-social-post-target="photoButton"
                 data-action="click->social-post#showPhotos"
                 <%= "disabled" if post.link.present? || post.photos.any? %>>
        <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "images") %>
        <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".add_photos") %></span>
      </wa-button>

      <%# The server writes the first value, thus the line has its height before the JavaScript
          runs.
          ⚠️ The number is the length of the text that BLUESKY will get, after the handles go in.
          SocialPresenter#bluesky_length makes it, and this view holds no count of its own. %>
      <%# ⚠️ The ring is `aria-hidden`: the words beside it say the same thing. The live region is a
          hidden span of its own, which the controller writes only when the count crosses the warning
          or the limit. %>
      <%# ⚠️ The ring is LAST, thus it does not move when the number beside it gets a digit. The count
          sits at the end of the row with `margin-inline-start: auto`, and NOT with `space-between`:
          it must stay there with the button hidden. %>
      <div class="social__count wa-caption-s" data-social-post-target="count">
        <span data-social-post-target="countText"><%= count %> / <%= limit %></span>
        <span class="wa-visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-social-post-target="countNotice"></span>
        <wa-progress-ring class="social__ring" aria-hidden="true"
                          value="<%= [ (count * 100.0 / limit).round, 100 ].min %>"
                          data-social-post-target="ring"></wa-progress-ring>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# The photos of the post: the picker, and one tile for each photo. ⚠️ The X of the picker
        shows only while the picker holds no photo: a picker that closes with tiles in it would
        still send them with the form. The server renders it open for a post that holds a photo.
        It needs a rule for `[hidden]`; refer to _social.scss. %>
    <div class="social-post__photos" data-social-post-target="photos"
         data-action="dragover->social-post#dragOverPhoto drop->social-post#dropPhoto"
         <%= "hidden" if post.photos.empty? %>>
      <div class="social-post__picker">
        <%# ⚠️ It has NO name: the files never go with the form. The controller uploads each one at
            the moment the owner picks it, then empties the input. It is disabled at the most
            photos. %>
        <wa-file-input class="social-post__file-input" accept="image/*" multiple size="small"
                       label="<%= t(".photos") %>" hint="<%= t(".photos_hint", count: max_photos, mastodon: Mastodon::MAX_MEDIA_ATTACHMENTS) %>"
                       data-social-post-target="fileInput"
                       data-action="change->social-post#filesPicked keydown.esc->social-post#hidePhotos"
                       <%= "disabled" if post.photos.length >= max_photos %>>
        </wa-file-input>

        <%# The way out of an empty picker, as the X of the link field. %>
        <wa-button class="social-post__picker-close" appearance="plain" size="small"
                   data-social-post-target="pickerClose"
                   data-action="click->social-post#hidePhotos"
                   <%= "hidden" if post.photos.any? %>>
          <%# ⚠️ `circle-xmark`, as the remove control of a post and of a photo tile has. The X
              inside the link field, and the one on the link card, stay a plain `xmark`: those two
              are inside another control. %>
          <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "circle-xmark") %>
          <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".close_photos") %></span>
        </wa-button>
      </div>

      <div class="social-post__tiles" data-social-post-target="tiles">
        <% post.photos.each do |photo| %>
          <%= render "photo", photo: photo, alt_text: alt_text %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%# ⚠️ One empty tile, which the controller clones. The browser renders none of a <template>,
        thus its fields are not in the form. This template is inside the template of a post, and a
        clone of that one carries this one with it. %>
    <template data-social-post-target="photoTemplate">
      <%= render "photo", photo: SocialPresenter::Photo.new, alt_text: alt_text %>
    </template>

    <%# ⚠️ The link is OPTIONAL and it has no `required`. There is no list of the articles here, on
        purpose: the card comes from the og: tags of whatever page this names.
        ⚠️ The server renders it open for a post that already holds a link, thus a page that renders
        again after a refusal shows that link.
        ⚠️ It needs a rule for `[hidden]`; refer to _social.scss. %>
    <wa-input class="social-post__link" type="url" name="posts[][link]" label="<%= t(".link") %>"
              value="<%= post.link %>"
              placeholder="<%= t(".link_placeholder") %>"
              autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
              data-social-post-target="link"
              data-action="input->social-post#schedulePreview change->social-post#schedulePreview
                           keydown.esc->social-post#removeLink blur->social-post#commitLink"
              <%= "hidden" if post.link.blank? %>>
      <%# It spins for the whole wait: the debounce and then the request. ⚠️ It needs a rule for
          `[hidden]`; refer to _social.scss. %>
      <wa-spinner slot="end" class="social__spinner" data-social-post-target="spinner" hidden></wa-spinner>

      <%# ⚠️ This is the one way out of the field, and it calls the same method as the X on the
          card. Without it, a field that the owner opened and left empty would stay open. The Escape
          key above does the same thing. %>
      <wa-button slot="end" class="social-post__link-remove" appearance="plain" size="small"
                 data-action="click->social-post#removeLink">
        <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "xmark") %>
        <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".remove_link") %></span>
      </wa-button>
    </wa-input>

    <%# The card of the link. The controller fills it and shows it, and it takes the place of the
        field above.
        ⚠️ It shows for EVERY link that this app could read a page for, and not only for a link that
        Bluesky will draw a card from. A page with no og: tags gets its address in place of a title.
        ⚠️ `with-media` is not in this markup: the controller sets it with the image. %>
    <wa-card class="social-card" data-social-post-target="preview" hidden>
      <img slot="media" class="social-card__image" data-social-post-target="previewImage" alt="" hidden>

      <%# ⚠️ The badge says that Bluesky will render the standard.site card. A card with NO badge is
          the ordinary card from the og: tags. %>
      <wa-badge class="social-card__kind" appearance="outlined" variant="success"
                data-social-post-target="previewKind" hidden></wa-badge>
      <p class="social-card__host wa-caption-s" data-social-post-target="previewHost"></p>
      <p class="social-card__title" data-social-post-target="previewTitle"></p>
      <p class="social-card__description" data-social-post-target="previewDescription"></p>

      <%# The two controls of the card, in its footer: Edit puts the field back with the link still
          in it, and Remove takes the link off the post.

          ⚠️ They are in the `footer` slot and NOT in `footer-actions`. The card draws a footer only
          when the `footer` slot holds something, thus `footer-actions` alone renders nothing, with
          no message. %>
      <div slot="footer" class="social-card__actions">
        <wa-button class="social-card__action" appearance="plain" size="small"
                   data-action="click->social-post#showLink">
          <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "pen-to-square") %>
          <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".edit_link") %></span>
        </wa-button>
        <wa-button class="social-card__action" appearance="plain" size="small"
                   data-action="click->social-post#removeLink">
          <%= raw icon_svg("classic", "light", "xmark") %>
          <span class="wa-visually-hidden"><%= t(".remove_link") %></span>
        </wa-button>
      </div>
    </wa-card>
  </div>
</div>
